:T10","usage":{"input_tokens":110240,"output_tokens":3459,"requests":6}},{"kind":"resumed","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"5943d2617eb532b1f5aee43d336f1d3edd8beb4bf13032b8453eea6a18a4a8b0"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":50523,"output_tokens":1966,"requests":4}},{"kind":"resumed","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"3defc6cc09d838c25352c097a7834c76ea5f66df27c6971b3a089e0a79cc8bd9"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":108510,"output_tokens":2416,"requests":5}},{"kind":"resumed","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"9c7a717635b69bd297b8cbd7684733e9b12060a1765589ac180095ea3e9ea21e"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T11","usage":{"input_tokens":7774,"output_tokens":491,"requests":1}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the empirical basis for MCP_MEM_MIN_MB (measure the mcp container's steady-state RSS on t4g.large and set the threshold to cover a 2x overlap plus headroom), or note a spike/measurement step that derives it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5833,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"`< MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` (default 1024) ABORTS\"","t4g.large 8 GiB box, 2x overlap of MCP containers during deploy","The plan does not state the MCP container's typical RSS, so 1024 cannot be checked against actual need — MemAvailable=1100 could pass yet still OOM a heavier container"],"finding":"The MCP_MEM_MIN_MB default of 1024 is an asserted threshold with no stated basis in the MCP container's actual memory footprint during the 2x overlap window; the pre-check guards against starting a second container but its correctness depends on the threshold reflecting the new container's expected RSS.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc0ee46433e06fdb6","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (Memory pre-check) — `MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` (default 1024)","norm_id":"n6ab4fe1ed6338fde","priority":0.3667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["MemAvailable sits just above 1024 but the new MCP container needs more, so both containers coexist and the box OOM-kills a serving/certified-op container despite the guard"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the mcp deploy path reconciles the nginx include and the managed set on a routine box reboot (not just rollback): whether the first post-reboot tick re-validates that the include's port has a live backend and re-flips/re-seeds if not, and how compose-mcp-1 + a surviving blue-green container are counted and reconciled.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.3487,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["materialize-mcp-upstream.sh installs the seed 'ONLY IF absent' and defers to a flip that 'may own it' (mcp-upstream.conf:9-11)","mcp service uses `--restart always` (docker-compose.yml:324) and the plan reproduces `--restart always` for `mcp_run_new`","compose-up.sh:197 re-runs materialize-mcp-upstream.sh and re-brings-up compose-mcp-1 on 8091 at boot","plan states 'autodeploy never `docker compose up mcp`' and only resets the include to 8091 as a ROLLBACK step, not on a routine reboot"],"finding":"The plan does not specify how the post-reboot state reconciles: after a deploy the nginx include points at 8092/8093 and materialize-mcp-upstream.sh leaves it untouched on the next boot, while compose-up.sh brings compose-mcp-1 back on 8091. Depending on whether the last blue-green container (with --restart always) or the compose-original survived the reboot, /mcp's include may name a freed/dead port until the next deploy, and the managed-set/port accounting sees both compose-mcp-1 and a blue-green container simultaneously.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4c8f42ec82aea159","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Run mechanism + managed set / Compat / rollback","norm_id":"n78d78c3a280bbed0","priority":0.2513,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Box reboots after an mcp deploy: include points at 8092, compose-mcp-1 comes up on 8091, the blue-green container on 8092 restarts (or was already rm'd, leaving 8092 with no backend)","Managed-set count on the first post-reboot tick sees both compose-mcp-1 and a blue-green container, affecting cap/sweep logic"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"ye